course: dictionary
lesson: 927
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around the word to find the clue. The word blessing is a good example.
explain: In church, «The priest gave a blessing at the end of the service» means a prayer asking God to protect and do good to people. Families may say a blessing before a meal, too. Here the clue is the church and the prayer.
explain: Now read «Her kindness was a blessing to us all.» Here blessing means something good that you are glad and thankful for. There is no prayer in this sentence, so the clue is the word good.
explain: Sometimes a phrase has its own meaning. «A blessing in disguise» means something that seems bad at first but turns out to be good. When you see a familiar word in a strange phrase, stop and check the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: A blessing can be a prayer asking God to protect and do good to someone.
fact: A blessing can be something good that you are glad and thankful for, as in «count your blessings».
fact: A blessing can mean permission or approval, as in «with my parents' blessing».
fact: «A blessing in disguise» means something that seems bad at first but turns out good.
fact: Christians believe blessings come from God. Other faiths and non-religious families also have their own ways of welcoming new life.
exercise: The priest gave a blessing at the end of the service. What is a blessing here? | *A prayer asking God to protect and do good to people | A bad thing that turns out good | A loud noise | A kind of hat
exercise: «We moved to the new house with our parents' blessing.» What does blessing mean here? | A gift wrapped in paper | Something that seems bad at first | *Permission or approval | A prayer about the weather
exercise: «Losing that match taught me a lesson, but it was a blessing in disguise.» What does this phrase mean? | A very dark and gloomy day | A blessing given in church | *Something bad that turns out to be good | Something that is always bad
test: «Be thankful: count your blessings.» What does this ask you to do? | Pray for a bad day to end | Forget about all the good things you have | *Be thankful for the good things in your life | Count the number of coins you own
test: The new baby was a blessing to the family. What does blessing suggest? | *Something good that the family is glad and thankful for | A prayer that the baby will be sad | A rule about naming days | A loud crying noise that stops
exam: Which sentence uses blessing to mean a prayer? | Her talent was a blessing to the whole team | It was a blessing in disguise that the bus was late | *The priest asked God to bless the families with a blessing | We had our parents' blessing to go
